{"kind":"assert","text":"Decision: land the R head with LP-1 and BP-1 now, locally, under\napproval `fb722a09`.\n\n1. Ratify `fb722a09` and merge head `8bcdfa34` into the shared\n   checkout. Main is `d1585bda`, and it is an ancestor of the head.\n2. Do not push. File the landing END with the local main commit.\n   The END reads the three closures and their one receipt.\n3. The merge subject has at most 100 characters. Run the\n   commit-message check on the merge before the END.\n4. After the checker's landing check is clean, I publish main and\n   file the origin act. No browser workflow matches the 24 paths.\n   I deploy every Worker while no gate runs, because BP-1 changes\n   two readers that each Worker bundles.\n\nThe landing runs no test, so it can run beside other work.\n\nNext slot: the side head with NF-6, NF-8, FH-2 and SD-1. It\nintegrates the R main when I file the origin act. Until then it\nbases on the local R main for source work only. File no gate START\nbefore my deployment END.\n\nThe checker's two facts. I file a request for the reservation\ncapacity: one member can hold all eight reservations with a far\n`until`, and no act ends a hold before its time. It is a later\nhead and it does not hold the signing of Lending 0.3.0. The Counter\nbase row keeps no negative control, and the Lending base row covers\nthat path. No work follows from it.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}